1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,200
Welcome back to the workshop. Today we
look at how captions are cut for phones.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,900
<i>Most subtitle files</i> were written for a wide
screen, with lines of forty characters or more.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,600
On a phone that becomes four or five short lines,
and nobody can read that fast.

4
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,300
{\an8}So we re-cut them: shorter lines, shorter cues,
and breaks that follow the sentence.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,000
Tom &amp; Sarah tested it on 12 videos.

6
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,900
The result was easier to read, and nobody
missed a word.
